```

To display a matrix as a bitmap with a zoom feature in Qt, you can use the QMatrix class to represent the matrix and the QPainter class to draw it on a QWidget. You can also implement a zoom function using the QTransform class. Here's an example of how to do this:

```cpp
#include <QApplication>
#include <QWidget>
#include <QMatrix>
#include <QPainter>
#include <QTransform>

class MatrixWidget : public QWidget {
    Q_OBJECT

public:
    MatrixWidget(QWidget *parent) : QWidget(parent) {}

protected:
    void paintEvent(QPaintEvent *event) override {
        QPainter painter(this);
        painter.setMatrix(matrix);
        painter.drawRect(0, 0, width(), height());
    }

public slots:
    void zoomIn() {
        matrix.scale(1.1, 1.1);
        update();
    }

    void zoomOut() {
        matrix.scale(0.9, 0.9);
        update();
    }

private:
    QMatrix matrix;
};

int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
    QApplication app(argc, argv);
    MatrixWidget widget;
    widget.show();
    return app.exec();
}
```

This code creates a QWidget that displays a matrix using the QPainter class. The matrix is represented by a QMatrix object, and the paintEvent function is called whenever the widget needs to be redrawn. The zoomIn and zoomOut slots are connected to buttons or other user interface elements that allow the user to zoom in and out of the matrix.

