1. Install the `cors` package in your Next.js project by running `npm install cors`.
2. Create a new file named `cors.js` in your `pages/api` directory.
3. Add the following code to the `cors.js` file:
```javascript
import { Cors } from 'cors';

const cors = new Cors({
  methods: ['GET', 'POST'],
  allowedHeaders: ['Content-Type', 'Authorization'],
  origin: 'https://your-wordpress-site.com' // Replace with your WordPress site URL
});

export default cors.createHandler({
  async handle(req, res) {
    await cors.handleRequest(req, res);

    if (req.method === 'OPTIONS') {
      res.statusCode = 200;
      res.json({ success: true });
    } else {
      // Handle your request logic here
    }
  },
});
```
1. Update your WordPress site's `wp-config.php` file to allow requests from your Next.js application. Add the following code to the `wp-config.php` file:
```php
define('WP_ALLOW_REST_REQUESTS', true);
define('WP_JSON_URL_PATH', '/wp-json');
```
1. Save both files and refresh your browser. You should now be able to make CORS requests from your Next.js application to your WordPress site without any errors.

