  for (let i = 1; i < arr.length; i++) { // Iterate through the remaining elements
    if (arr[i] > max) { // Check if the current element is greater than the maximum value
      max = arr[i]; // Update the maximum value if it is
    }
  }
  return max; // Return the maximum value
}
```

This algorithm takes an array as input and returns the maximum element in the array. It works by initializing the maximum value as the first element, then iterating through the remaining elements and updating the maximum value if a larger element is found. Finally, it returns the maximum value.

